author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "pm context TOON focus tables omit empty json_columns and absent arrays and a decoder recognizes the block by its reserved collection_encoding key name; decodePmTableRows restores rows exactly from a block without json_columns or absent, and still decodes every block shape earlier releases emitted; Missing cells use an encoding no larger than the pair list on the pm context corpus, and round-trip tests cover sparse, null, list and nested columns; null_columns and list_columns stay declared so explicit nulls and list cells remain distinguishable, and JSON output is unchanged; A spec measures pm context --limit 20 TOON encoding bytes against the 2026.11.7 baseline and fails on regression, and release notes carry a migration line for TOON table decoders"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: medium
reporter: unbraind
severity: low
repro_steps: "On this repository's tracker at main 70c14d4a3 (3,230 items, blocked and unblocked open items present), run pm context --limit 20 and compare the bytes of the high_level_encoding and low_level_encoding blocks with the total TOON output; pm context --limit 5 emits only the high_level_encoding block"
resolution: "projectPmTableEncodingForToon (src/sdk/output/table-rows.ts) drops an empty json_columns and an empty absent list and groups absent coordinates into absent_rows (column to row indexes); the TOON host applies it to both table candidates before choosing the smallest rendering. decodePmTableRows takes the new exported PmRenderedTableCellEncoding (json_columns and absent optional, absent_rows added) and still decodes pair lists and legacy column_order; encodePmTableRows' return contract is unchanged. Blocks are recognized by the reserved <collection>_encoding key. null_columns and list_columns stay declared; JSON is unchanged. SDK surface signature change acknowledged as a widening; contract_change carries the TOON decoder migration line."
expected_result: "pm context TOON carries no empty encoding arrays and encodes missing cells densely, so encoding metadata is a small fraction of the read while every JSON fact stays decodable"
actual_result: "This tracker's pm context --limit 20: encoding metadata 618 -> 310 B; spec corpus 638 -> 331 B, ratcheted at 331; fast-check round trip through the TOON projection for compact and plain encodings; legacy blocks decode exactly"
