comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-13T07:57:03.384Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence (2026-11-13): encodePmTableRows keeps returning json_columns and absent (no SDK return-type change). The TOON host passes each candidate's encoding through projectPmTableEncodingForToon, which drops an empty json_columns and an empty absent list and groups absent coordinates by column in absent_rows. decodePmTableRows accepts the new exported PmRenderedTableCellEncoding (json_columns and absent optional, absent_rows added) and still decodes pair lists and legacy column_order. The SDK surface gate classifies the widened parameter as a signature change; acknowledged in sdk/public-surface.json because every PmEncodedTableRows argument stays valid. null_columns and list_columns stay declared. Measured: this tracker's pm context --limit 20 encoding metadata 618 -> 310 B (whole read 8,721 -> 8,224 B with the GH-1703 receipt change); spec corpus 638 -> 331 B, ratcheted at 331. Search blocks now carry only list_columns. Caveat recorded in the docstring: grouping is smaller whenever a column misses more than one cell; one absent cell under a key that needs quoting can cost a byte more, so the claim is scoped to the context corpus, as the AC is."
